# A companion in the party does not stop a fight from ending — killing the last enemy still wins it.
#
# The question this answers is whether FightState.CheckFightEnd can mistake a companion for an enemy
# and sit waiting for them to fall. It cannot be answered with `fight-end victory`, which sets the
# result directly and never evaluates the condition — so this one is played out blow by blow, and the
# ONLY thing that can end it is anyEnemyAlive going false with a second party fighter still standing.
# Reaching WorldView is therefore the assertion; there is no weaker way to make it.
#
# --fill-party is what puts a companion in the roster: at seed 42 that is the cat Nighthunter, who
# joins the fight as a party fighter (BuildFighters walks Protagonist.CompanionParty). `expect` on the
# initiative panel below is what stops this quietly degrading into a solo fight if that ever changes.
#
# --grant-mm arms the protagonist: unarmed skills are gated behind their modi mentis and a fresh
# character knows none of the attacking ones, so without it Kenryc can only end his turn.
#
# The loop is turn-agnostic on purpose. Both attacks are offered every round and only the one the
# active fighter actually knows lands; the other reports `error: no usable or learnable skill`, which
# is noise rather than a failure (a CLI error does not fail a run — only `expect` and `wait` do).
# Six rounds is margin: at this seed the wolf falls in four.
#
# Note `strategy succeed` pins EVERY attacker's dice, the wolf's included, so this is a race the
# protagonist wins only because the run is seeded. If it ever starts ending in death, that is the
# reason, and the fix is more grants rather than fewer rounds.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --grant-mm pugilitas:5,brawling:5 --start-fight wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode Fighting 90

# The companion is really in this fight, and on the party's side of it: the initiative panel marks
# party fighters with ☻ and enemies with ☹.
expect ☻ Nighthunt
expect ☹ Redhorn

strategy succeed

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

state
click skill "Lacerate"
click skill "Knee Strike"
wait 25
click fighter Redhorn
wait 25
click continue
wait 25
click end-turn
wait 35

# The wolf is down and the fight let go of the game. Had the companion been counted an enemy, the
# fight would still be running here and this would time out in Fighting.
wait mode WorldView 60
wait 30

# The companion came out of it still in the party — a fight that ended by killing the wrong side
# would have taken them out of it.
inspect party
expect-state party Nighthunter

quit
